    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0380" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">610.1131/312½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-15">June 15, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am anxious to get in
                    specific form from the several departments that are concerned with our economic
                    relations with Latin America, the combined judgment of the Secretaries of the
                    Departments of State, Treasury, Agriculture and Commerce relative to the action
                    which this government should take. I am enclosing a copy of one of the many
                    memoranda I have received relating to this subject.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d437-f1"/></p>
                <pb facs="0381" n="369" xml:id="pg369"/>
                <p>Inasmuch as the matter is of great urgency I request that you report to me not
                    later than Thursday, June 20.</p>
                <p>I wish you would take the initiative in calling this group together.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D.
                    Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
